<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus quagga Holocene Turing wavelength at 1.9 mm (detail s0) — MorphoEval overall 85.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg kinetics with anteroposterior-biased inhibitor diffusion on a periodic flank window of ten fastest-mode wavelengths. The length unit is pinned so lambda(k_fast) = 1.883 mm (log10 = -2.725) at gamma = 1.15, age 0 Ma. Bard 1977 initiation spacing is 0.40 mm; the growth factor 4.707 is reconstructed. A gamma sweep gives Pearson r = 0.997 and RMSE = 0.067 mm between analytical k_fast and the nonlinear FFT. The nominal FFT sits at 2.03 mm because the periodic domain snaps to an integer mode. Equal diffusion (Equus scotti control) returns the field to the homogeneous state (amplitude 3e-6 versus 3.65). The Namutoni flank crop (CC BY-SA 3.0) and the rendered GIF share near-vertical stripes; the simulation breaks into dashes and the photo is an adult animal, so this is a pattern-class match, not a pixel identity. Overall 85.5/100 (faithfulness 85.0, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/equus_quagga_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 553458 B, 1512×888 px, artifact_sha256 63bb5de23ed6cd3e54c0be79e5812c07a0a9ce980568ce526d68bb970186e97a (sha256 63bb5de23ed6cd3e54c0be79e5812c07a0a9ce980568ce526d68bb970186e97a), spec_fingerprint c15e608fbebdc00810bdf416a1196b656433143dafaa4373228dabec7a265ec8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c15e608fbebdc00810bdf416a1196b656433143dafaa4373228dabec7a265ec8; artifact_sha256: 63bb5de23ed6cd3e54c0be79e5812c07a0a9ce980568ce526d68bb970186e97a. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used here. | Murray 1981: a reaction-diffusion pre-pattern for mammalian coat markings. | Bard 1977: plains-zebra stripes are about 0.4 mm apart and perpendicular to the dorsal line in the third embryonic week.; reconstructed_in_script: The 1.883 mm detail length is the slot scale, obtained by pinning the fastest ky=0 mode, not a new measurement on a fetus. | Growth factor 4.707 = 1.883/0.40 is reconstructed. Anisotropic inhibitor diffusion stands in for the orientation Bard described and Staddon 2024 modelled with curvature; curvature itself is not solved. | Equus scotti is represented only as the equal-diffusion ablation. Its coat is not known from this run.; transfer_boundary: The wildlife photograph is an adult flank at centimetre scale. It tests orientation and contrast, not the 1.883 mm fetal wavelength.; does_not_claim: Does not claim 1.883 mm was calipered on a named Equus quagga specimen in this loop. | Does not claim Equus scotti was the direct anagenetic ancestor, only the assigned chronoseries predecessor. | Does not claim the broken Schnakenberg dashes are the adult stripe geometry. | Does not claim a second assessor scored this pass.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Only one flank crop is segmented. Add a second body region and report its period and angle separately.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Nominal FFT wavelength is 2.03 mm against analytical 1.883 mm (integer mode on the periodic window). State that quantization in the fit rather than letting the headline lambda hide it, or refine the grid until the mode is closer.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Schnakenberg stripes break into dashes. Test whether a stronger anteroposterior anisotropy, or an explicit stripe-stabilizing term, joins them without dropping the specimen CV match.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Single builder-assessor. An independent second score is still open.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.55e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus quagga Holocene Turing wavelength at 1.9 mm (detail s0) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Raising gamma shortens both the analytical and the PDE wavelength together (r = 0.997). Setting the diffusion ratio to 1 extinguishes the pattern. Anisotropy is a real parameter but is not itself swept in the figure." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

